# 🚀 Two-Tier Flask Application Deployment on AWS EKS

## 📌 Project Overview
This project demonstrates the deployment of a two-tier web application using Kubernetes on AWS EKS.

- Frontend: Flask (Python)
- Backend: MySQL
- Orchestration: Kubernetes (AWS EKS)

The application is deployed using Kubernetes Deployments and exposed via a LoadBalancer service.

---

## 🏗 Architecture

User → AWS LoadBalancer → Flask App (Pod) → MySQL Service → MySQL Pod

---

## ⚙️ Tech Stack

- Docker
- Kubernetes (EKS)
- AWS
- Python (Flask)
- MySQL
- kubectl
- YAML

---

## 🔥 Features

- Multi-tier application deployment
- Service-to-service communication using Kubernetes DNS (mysql-svc)
- External access using LoadBalancer
- Debugging of real-world issues (CrashLoopBackOff, DB errors)
- Database initialization and management

